# Hash-locked closure for .github/workflows/test.yml (ubuntu + windows,
# Python 3.11-3.13; one universal lock). It repeats, with the same specifiers,
# [project].dependencies plus the dev, sign and openislet extras of
# pyproject.toml and the [build-system] backend, so the package itself installs
# with --no-deps --no-build-isolation -e . and nothing is resolved unhashed.
# tests/test_ci_requirements.py fails if this file, the lock or the workflow
# drift apart.
#
# Regenerate after editing (or after a pyproject.toml dependency change):
#   uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.11 --generate-hashes \
#     requirements/ci/test.in -o requirements/ci/test.txt
